@kdy1 It looks like the problem is that swc binds `this` to the output function declaration.

```javascript
MyClass.prototype.init = (function(param1) {
    var _ref = _asyncToGenerator(regeneratorRuntime.mark(function _callee(param1) {
        // Function body omitted because it's not important
    }).bind(this)); // <-- Here
    return function() {
        return _ref.apply(this, arguments);
    };
})();
```

Note that babel gets this right and correctly does not add `.bind(this)` to the `_asyncToGenerator` function.

My intuition is that the solution is to not bind `this` for async functions defined on the `prototype` object, but I don't see an easy way in `ecmascript/transforms/compat/src/es2017/async_to_generator.rs` to tell if the function expression is defined on a prototype. Any thoughts on how to handle this?

